{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "20284",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 1.33,
      "end_seconds": 4.77,
      "duration_seconds": 3.44,
      "text": "hello, sorry about the delay, do sit"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 6.47,
      "end_seconds": 11.86,
      "duration_seconds": 5.39,
      "text": "Doctor, I'm just here to help with the details."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 14.66,
      "end_seconds": 20.77,
      "duration_seconds": 6.11,
      "text": "yes, that's no problem at all please sit start wherever you like, I'm listening"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 22.3,
      "end_seconds": 29.44,
      "duration_seconds": 7.14,
      "text": "Erm, it's the room spinning, doctor. She didn't want to come, but I insisted."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 30.4,
      "end_seconds": 33.37,
      "duration_seconds": 2.97,
      "text": "has this been going on for long?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 34.68,
      "end_seconds": 40.52,
      "duration_seconds": 5.84,
      "text": "Around ten days... no wait, it's more like two days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 41.94,
      "end_seconds": 52.31,
      "duration_seconds": 10.37,
      "text": "Tell me a bit more about it: how bad it gets, how often, and whether anything makes it better or worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 57.89,
      "end_seconds": 67.92,
      "duration_seconds": 10.03,
      "text": "yes, turning my head that makes it worse it's severe, honestly it just comes and goes"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 69.51,
      "end_seconds": 71.88,
      "duration_seconds": 2.37,
      "text": "Any nausea and vomiting as well?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 72.38,
      "end_seconds": 99.6,
      "duration_seconds": 27.22,
      "text": "Yes, actually. Um, about nausea and vomiting, it comes and goes. There's being unsteady as well. Sorry, what was I saying, with being unsteady, about a seven out of ten. Mm, I did have a recent cold at one point, but that's gone now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 100.78,
      "end_seconds": 103.81,
      "duration_seconds": 3.03,
      "text": "time for your numbers, if that's okay"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 110.66,
      "end_seconds": 112.72,
      "duration_seconds": 2.06,
      "text": "Sit still for a moment..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 125.33,
      "end_seconds": 132.11,
      "duration_seconds": 6.78,
      "text": "Okay: BP is 119 over 71, pulse is 77 beats a minute, temperature 36.5."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 134.18,
      "end_seconds": 137.48,
      "duration_seconds": 3.3,
      "text": "Could you come over to the couch, please?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 144.51,
      "end_seconds": 145.66,
      "duration_seconds": 1.15,
      "text": "Of course."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 147.56,
      "end_seconds": 149.5,
      "duration_seconds": 1.94,
      "text": "hold that for a second"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 164.21,
      "end_seconds": 172.8,
      "duration_seconds": 8.59,
      "text": "I can see a fine jerking of the eyes to the left and your walking is a little unsteady."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 178.4,
      "end_seconds": 186.03,
      "duration_seconds": 7.63,
      "text": "Please sit back down. Have you noticed slurred speech, ringing in the ears, hearing loss or headache?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 187.27,
      "end_seconds": 190.74,
      "duration_seconds": 3.47,
      "text": "No, none of those at all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 191.25,
      "end_seconds": 193.9,
      "duration_seconds": 2.65,
      "text": "Did you notice any double vision?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 194.54,
      "end_seconds": 198.6,
      "duration_seconds": 4.06,
      "text": "I mean, I haven't noticed any double vision."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 199.37,
      "end_seconds": 201.78,
      "duration_seconds": 2.41,
      "text": "Has your skin been okay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 202.43,
      "end_seconds": 203.45,
      "duration_seconds": 1.02,
      "text": "Skin's normal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 218.03,
      "end_seconds": 221.85,
      "duration_seconds": 3.82,
      "text": "Let me ask about allergies, anything at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 223.17,
      "end_seconds": 228.64,
      "duration_seconds": 5.47,
      "text": "Yes, tramadol. I get feeling very drowsy. Yes, trimethoprim."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 229.62,
      "end_seconds": 232.06,
      "duration_seconds": 2.44,
      "text": "Do you have any chronic illnesses?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 235.46,
      "end_seconds": 240.86,
      "duration_seconds": 5.4,
      "text": "I've, I've got high blood pressure. I've got epilepsy."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 244.89,
      "end_seconds": 256.59,
      "duration_seconds": 11.7,
      "text": "Alright, high blood pressure and epilepsy, that matches what I have here. So, tell me about your routine, work, habits, that sort of thing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 257.69,
      "end_seconds": 276.73,
      "duration_seconds": 19.04,
      "text": "I've never touched a cigarette. I'll have a glass of wine with dinner. I work in accounts at a hospital. My partner and our baby. I drink a lot of tea and snack through the day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 277.28,
      "end_seconds": 280.21,
      "duration_seconds": 2.93,
      "text": "What's on your current medicine list?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 285.98,
      "end_seconds": 289.41,
      "duration_seconds": 3.43,
      "text": "Amlodipine, 5 milligrams, once a day"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 290.75,
      "end_seconds": 302.9,
      "duration_seconds": 12.15,
      "text": "Hmm, doctor, I think the last prescription for the amlodipine was 2.5 milligrams. We changed it at the last visit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 304.47,
      "end_seconds": 309.8,
      "duration_seconds": 5.33,
      "text": "Okay. Have you got the newest prescription or the the box with you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 310.4,
      "end_seconds": 319.35,
      "duration_seconds": 8.95,
      "text": "erm, you know, no, I left it at home. Carbamazepine, 200 milligrams, twice a day"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 319.88,
      "end_seconds": 322.4,
      "duration_seconds": 2.52,
      "text": "Roughly how long on that one?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 323.02,
      "end_seconds": 325.31,
      "duration_seconds": 2.29,
      "text": "Nearly five years now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 326.55,
      "end_seconds": 341.78,
      "duration_seconds": 15.23,
      "text": "so, based on the history and the examination, this looks most like an inner-ear balance problem such as vestibular neuritis. I'd also keep a problem in the brain stem in mind"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 343.81,
      "end_seconds": 347.28,
      "duration_seconds": 3.47,
      "text": "Do you think it's something serious?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 348.49,
      "end_seconds": 359.68,
      "duration_seconds": 11.19,
      "text": "it's reasonable to be concerned, but right now an inner-ear balance problem such as vestibular neuritis is my leading thought, not anything worse"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 369.68,
      "end_seconds": 400.76,
      "duration_seconds": 31.08,
      "text": "I think a positional test makes sense here, for vertigo. I think blood tests makes sense here, for dizziness. I'd like you to take prochlorperazine, 5 milligrams, three times a day, for three days. You take it by mouth. It's for nausea and vertigo. It's a commonly used medicine and most people tolerate it well. Start moving around gently as soon as you can, since resting too long slows recovery."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 402.47,
      "end_seconds": 410.93,
      "duration_seconds": 8.46,
      "text": "and please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 412.8,
      "end_seconds": 414.48,
      "duration_seconds": 1.68,
      "text": "Okay, makes sense."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 419.98,
      "end_seconds": 424.19,
      "duration_seconds": 4.21,
      "text": "is there anything you'd like me to go over again?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 424.72,
      "end_seconds": 426.69,
      "duration_seconds": 1.97,
      "text": "That's clear, thanks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 428.58,
      "end_seconds": 429.88,
      "duration_seconds": 1.3,
      "text": "goodbye for now"
    }
  ]
}